{"name":"Capocollo","hex":"#d9544d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"capocollo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of cured pork sausage"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capocollo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Capocollo","blocks":[{"text":"Capocollo or coppa is an Italian pork salted meat made from the dry-cured muscle running from the neck to the fourth or fifth rib of the pig shoulder or neck. It is whole-muscle, dry cured, and typically sliced very thinly. It is similar to the more widely known cured ham (prosciutto), because they are both pork-derived cold cuts used in similar dishes. It is not brined as ham typically is."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Coppa_di_Parma.jpg/330px-Coppa_di_Parma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capocollo"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sweetcapicola.JPG/250px-Sweetcapicola.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sweetcapicola.JPG/500px-Sweetcapicola.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sweetcapicola.JPG/250px-Sweetcapicola.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweetcapicola.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Capocollo_di_martina.jpg/250px-Capocollo_di_martina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Capocollo_di_martina.jpg/500px-Capocollo_di_martina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Capocollo_di_m